Phase 3.1 Cancellation Verification Report
==========================================

TESTS: test_cancel_moves_non_terminal_task_to_cancelled,
       test_cancel_of_terminal_task_changes_nothing,
       test_cancel_while_executing_requests_without_claiming_stop

CANCELLATION PATHS VERIFIED
----------------------------
1. Non-terminal task -> CANCELLED
   - aj.tasks.create() then aj.cancel_task()
   - Outcome: ok=True, status=CANCELLED
   - aj.cancel() returns False (already CANCELLED)

2. Terminal task (COMPLETED) -> no change
   - aj.handle("done") then aj.cancel_task()
   - Outcome: ok=False, status=COMPLETED (unchanged)
   - Respects terminal state boundary

3. EXECUTING task -> CANCEL_REQUESTED
   - Task progresses through UNDERSTANDING -> PLANNED -> AUTHORIZED -> EXECUTING
   - aj.cancel_task() while EXECUTING
   - Outcome: ok=False, status=CANCEL_REQUESTED
   - Summary contains "not interrupted"
   - requires_user_decision=True
   - Second aj.cancel_task() confirmation -> CANCELLED

CANCEL_REQUESTED SEMANTICS
--------------------------
- Honest message: "the running execution was not interrupted"
- No forced termination of external work
- Operator must explicitly confirm to transition to CANCELLED
- Requires user decision - intentional operator action

LEASE-BASED CANCELLATION
------------------------
- cancel_task() acquires lease with "cancel" operation
- hold() context manager ensures mutual exclusion
- Second operator attempting cancel gets LeaseHeld error
- Release returns lease to free state
- break_stale requires expired lease + operator action

EXIT CODES: 
- EXIT_CANCELLED (4): task was cancelled
- EXIT_FAILURE (2): cancel refused (terminal task)